# Route 2 for backlog row 19: a project that carries modelPath itself.
#
# The Fusion route is closed (resolve-fusion-path.log): effect.GetFusionComp()
# returns None and a comp on the item refuses the OFX node. Route 2 is the other
# candidate - a .drp that already carries the parameter, loaded with
# `poc.py --project`, rendered, and compared with the source.
#
# Answer: the .drp cannot carry it, and the reason is measured, not assumed.

## 1. what ExportProject writes in Resolve Studio 21.2.0.5

manager.ExportProject(projectName, "/abs/path/modelpath")   -> True
The result is a ZIP, 27003 bytes:

  project.xml                              18174
  MediaPool/Master/MpFolder.xml            35847
  SeqContainer/09a35342-...-d28ca8de.xml    3900
  Gallery.xml                               8915

## 2. the effect is not in the export

Right before the export, in the same session:

  item.GetEffects("ofx") -> 1 effect, name "ONNX Inference"

In the exported sequence XML the clip carries:

  <EffectFiltersBA/>
  <ImportExportMetadataBA/>

i.e. an empty effect list. `project.SaveProject` is not callable in this version
(`TypeError: 'NoneType' object is not callable`), so there is no "save first, then
export" variant that could write it: the host saves on its own schedule and the
export still drops the effect.

The fields that would hold the parameters are hex blobs (`FieldsBlob`,
`EffectFiltersBA`), not readable XML, so hand-writing a value in is not a route
either - the same conclusion §5 of resolve-automation.md reaches from the
container side, now with a filename and a size behind it.

## 3. what `poc.py --project` did once it ran

The mode had never run, and running it found four defects, all fixed:

  - `render_size` was only assigned in the --build-project branch, so --project
    would have died on an undefined name before the first render;
  - `facts["resolve"]` was set only when --resolve was passed, so any run without
    it died with `KeyError: 'resolve'` after installing the bundle;
  - `connect()` demanded an open project, and a host started with -nogui that has
    no last project sits on the project manager forever - `require_project=False`
    is the way out (it also stops a second Resolve.exe, which exits at once,
    counting as a dead host while the first one still answers);
  - `LoadProject` wants an absolute path: a relative ".validation/drp/saved.drp"
    that exists is refused ("could not load project"), the same trap
    SetRenderSettings has with TargetDir.

With those fixed, a run reached: validate, install, launch, connect (35 s),
gpu ("Compute API set to automatic, defaulting to CUDA"), load -> refused, then
the absolute-path fix. The runs after that fix did not get a scriptable host
again in two attempts (300 s and 600 s to the timeout, `-nogui` start), which is
the known unreliable start, not a result about the .drp.

## 4. bringing the archive back: import yes, load no

`poc.py --project` calls `ProjectManager.LoadProject(path)`. On the exported file
that answers **None** - twice, once with a relative and once with an absolute
path. The other door exists:

  LoadProject(abs)   -> None
  ImportProject(abs) -> True
  project name inside the archive: drp-roundtrip.Cfg
  GetCurrentProject() right after the import -> "Untitled Project", no timeline

So an exported project comes back only through ImportProject, and that leaves an
imported project that still has to be opened by its stored name ("<name>.Cfg",
with the extension). The attempt to load it by name did not finish: the two runs
after the absolute-path fix did not get a scriptable host again (300 s and 600 s
to the timeout, `-nogui` start), so "ImportProject then LoadProject(\"drp-roundtrip\")"
is written down as the next step, not as a result.

## 5. conclusion for row 19

Route 2 does not exist on this host: the effect an exported project would have to
carry is not exported at all, so a .drp made here cannot set modelPath. Producing
one needs the effect and the parameter typed into the GUI inspector, and even then
the state lands in a binary blob - which no runner can produce or verify without
clicking.

What would close row 19 is therefore one of:
  - a GUI-made .drp on a machine with a display, exported and committed, and a
    harness that only loads it (the load path is now measured up to LoadProject);
  - a host whose effect object exposes GetParam/SetParam;
  - a plug-in default that is not identity - already possible through
    -DREFERENCE_GAIN_DEFAULT / -DGAIN_DEFAULT for the gain templates, and the
    reason the ONNX template's GPU path stays unproven is that its default has no
    such switch.

## 6. the step section 4 left open, run on the same host

Bundle: `.validation/build-provider-only` (OFXPLUGIN_BUNDLE_ONNX_RUNTIME=OFF,
OFXPLUGIN_BUNDLE_CUDA_PROVIDER=ON, OFXPLUGIN_CUDA_FROM_HOST=ON, ONNX Runtime
1.20.1), installed into `C:\Program Files\Common Files\OFX\Plugins`, with
`Contents/Resources/model.onnx` beside the binary - the plug-in reads
`ONNX_MODEL_PATH` first and that file second, once at instance creation.

  pm.CreateProject("row19"); still resolve-source.png, 1920x1080
  item.AddEffect("ofx", "Open FX/OFX Plugin Developer/ONNX Inference")
  item.GetEffects("ofx") -> 1, GetInfo().name "ONNX Inference"
  render before the export -> JobStatus Complete, 100%, 3769 ms,
       frames-row19/row19-before00108149.png, 235070 bytes

  pm.ExportProject("row19", "…/.validation/drp/row19-import")      -> True
  file: row19-import.drp, 27219 bytes; its SeqContainer XML carries
    <EffectFiltersBA>000000020000007b8128b52ffd20…</EffectFiltersBA>
  whose hex spells out `com.ofxplugindeveloper.onnxinference` and
  `OfxImageEffectContextFilter`. This export DID carry the applied effect, unlike
  the one in section 2.

  pm.ImportProject("…/row19-import.drp")                            -> True
  pm.GetProjectListInCurrentFolder() contains "row19" and "row19-import"
  pm.LoadProject("row19-import")                                    -> project object
       GetName() -> "row19-import"; GetCurrentTimeline().GetName() -> "row19";
       GetItemListInTrack("video", 1) -> 1 item; GetEffects("ofx") -> 1
  render from the opened project -> Complete, 100%, 3273 ms,
       frames-row19/row19-after00108149.png, 235070 bytes

No `"<name>.Cfg"` appeared: the stored name is the file's base name and
`LoadProject` accepts it. The step section 4 called "the one nobody has
completed" is completed - `ImportProject` followed by `LoadProject(<base name>)`
opens the imported project, effect included.

What it does not prove is the frame. Both PNGs are identical to the source
(`mae 0.0`, `max_pixel 0`, 8294400 bytes compared), before and after the round
trip, because the host never instantiated the plug-in. `ResolveDebug.txt`, same
session:

  Could not get plugin handle for effect[com.ofxplugindeveloper.onnxinference]
    with context[OfxImageEffectContextFilter]                      2240 times
  Create context [OfxImageEffectContextFilter_…] failed for plugin […]
  Plugin [com.ofxplugindeveloper.onnxinference] is not available!!!!
  OFX: loading com.ofxplugindeveloper.onnxinference
  describe failed on plugin com.ofxplugindeveloper.onnxinference, error code 4

Not the model path and not the round trip: the same refusal appears with the
18-file full bundle (22:28:06) and with the source as it was before
`ONNX_MODEL_PATH` existed, built from the stashed tree (22:25:49). The fake host
describes and instantiates the same binaries - 84 contract checks over three host
profiles - so the difference is the real host. Error code 4 is what the OFX
Support library returns when a describe throws `HostInadequate` or
`PropertyUnknownToHost`.

So section 5's conclusion moves: a project exported here CAN carry the effect,
and the imported project opens by name. What blocks row 19's render is that
Resolve 21.2.0.5 will not describe this plug-in at all.
